@startuml sequence
title EAP-DID Authentication Exchange (Overview)\nFigure 2 -- see model-d-sequence-complete.puml for cryptographic detail

skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

actor "EAP Peer\n(supplicant)" as Supp
participant "Authenticator\n(802.1X PAE)" as AP
participant "EAP Server\n(EAP-DID)" as AAA
participant "Verifier" as Verifier
database "Verifiable Data\nRegistry" as Ledger

note over Supp
  The peer holds the VC and the subject signing key
  from enrolment and constructs the presentation
  locally. No Holder agent is reachable at this point.
end note

== Presentation Request ==

AAA -> AAA : challenge = base64url(random(24 octets))\n<i>generated per authentication exchange</i>
AAA -> Verifier : POST presentation invitation\n{schemaId, trustIssuers,\n options{challenge, domain}}
Verifier -> Verifier : mint did:peer for this exchange
Verifier -> AAA : {thid, invitationUrl, myDid}
AAA -> Verifier : retrieve X25519 private key for myDid\n<i>non-normative key service</i>
Verifier -> AAA : JWK {kty:"OKP", crv:"X25519", d, x}
AAA -> AP : EAP-Request/DID (fragment 1..N)
AP -> Supp : EAP-Request/DID (fragment 1..N)
Supp -> AP : EAP-Response/DID (fragment ACK)
AP -> AAA : EAP-Response/DID

== Presentation ==

Supp -> Supp : construct VP JWT [RFC7519]\nalg=ES256K [RFC8812]\niss = VC "sub"; aud = domain;\nnonce = challenge; jti; iat; exp
Supp -> Supp : encapsulate in DIDComm message;\nencrypt as JWE [RFC7516]\nECDH-1PU + A256KW + A256CBC-HS512\nCEK = random(64 octets), retained
Supp -> AP : EAP-Response/DID\ngzip(JWE) [RFC1952], fragment 1..N
AP -> AAA : EAP-Response/DID (reassembled)

== Validation ==

AAA -> AAA : unwrap Verifier recipient entry\n-> recover the same CEK\n<i>AES Key Wrap fails on key mismatch</i>
AAA -> Verifier : POST JWE\n(application/didcomm-encrypted+json)
Verifier -> Verifier : JWE decryption; extract VP JWT
Verifier -> Ledger : resolve issuer DID;\nretrieve credential status
Ledger -> Verifier : DID document; status
Verifier -> Verifier : validate signature, holder binding,\nvalidity period, challenge, domain,\nschema, trusted issuers, revocation
Verifier -> AAA : PresentationVerified

== Key Derivation ==

Supp -> Supp : MSK, EMSK = HKDF(CEK, salt=thid) [RFC5869]
AAA -> AAA : MSK, EMSK = HKDF(CEK, salt=thid) [RFC5869]

note over Supp, AAA
  The CEK is never transmitted over the EAP channel.
  Each side obtains it independently: the peer generates
  it when constructing the JWE; the EAP server recovers it
  by unwrapping the recipient entry. The thid is unique per
  exchange and is used as the HKDF salt, so repeated
  presentations of the same credential yield distinct keys.
end note

== Completion ==

AAA -> AP : EAP-Success [RFC3748]
AP -> Supp : EAP-Success\n(4-Way Handshake follows on IEEE 802.11 media)

note over Supp, Ledger
  The Issuer does not participate in this exchange. It is
  contacted once during enrolment (Figure 4). Only its DID
  is resolved here, and only by the Verifier.
  --
  <b>Model D limitation.</b> The Verifier did:peer is conveyed
  in band within the invitation and is not authenticated to
  the peer. An adversarial Authenticator can substitute its
  own identifier and read the presentation. It cannot replay
  the presentation elsewhere: nonce and aud bind it to this
  exchange, and exp bounds its lifetime.
end note

@enduml
